{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit","id":1146919,"title":"Why the Union does not nuke its enemies from orbit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-05T00:03:41-07:00","id":1146919,"title":"Why the Union does not nuke its enemies from orbit?","content":"Why the Union, especially Conventions like the Iteration X and the Void Engineers do not nuke every Haven, Caern, Pit, Hive, Haunts, Trods and Labyrinth from geostationary orbit? It is the simplest and most efficient and inexpensive(at least in terms of manpower and material losses) method to eradicate Methuselahs, Nephandi, BSD, Unseelie and other vile monstrosities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 10-05-2017, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T00:45:45-07:00","id":1146924,"title":"","content":"Because the bazzlion dollar orbit weapon would explode because of paradox after the first caern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T00:53:40-07:00","id":1146928,"title":"","content":"Nuking every mystical hotspot on the planet is pretty much *nuking the entire planet*. It's handing the Nephandi the win. As far as the Masses are concerned, it looks like someone's just started a nuclear war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T01:17:02-07:00","id":1146930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1146924#post1146924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the bazzlion dollar orbit weapon would explode because of paradox after the first caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Union can selectively bombard caerns on countrysides, jungles, forests, mountain ranges, oceans, polar regions, and other non-Paradoxical &quot;white zones.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 10-05-2017, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T01:17:36-07:00","id":1146931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1146928#post1146928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nuking every mystical hotspot on the planet is pretty much *nuking the entire planet*. It's handing the Nephandi the win. As far as the Masses are concerned, it looks like someone's just started a nuclear war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Union could nuke sites located outside of the Masses' collective perception. Vast majority of magickal and mystical hotspots and wellsprings are situated in the least populated areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 10-05-2017, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T01:24:50-07:00","id":1146936,"title":"","content":"Presumably the same reason the USA doesn't use nukes against ISIS. They tend to kill everything around them and leave the area permanently damaged. The latter is doubly so for the World of Darkness where they tend to blow holes in the Umbra and spiritually poison the local area.<br /> <br /> Also, the Technos aren't monsters (generally). There's a difference between their brand of subtle hypocrisy and blatant mass murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T01:27:44-07:00","id":1146938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1146936#post1146936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably the same reason the USA doesn't use nukes against ISIS. They tend to kill everything around them and leave the area permanently damaged. The latter is doubly so for the World of Darkness where they tend to blow holes in the Umbra and spiritually poison the local area.<br /> <br /> Also, the Technos aren't monsters (generally). There's a difference between their brand of subtle hypocrisy and blatant mass murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if that &quot;mass murdering atrocity&quot; means eradicating horrible, hideous monsters putting ISIS to shame?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T01:34:37-07:00","id":1146939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1146931#post1146931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Union could nuke sites located outside of the Masses' collective perception. Vast majority of magickal and mystical hotspots and wellsprings are in the least populated areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem with that reasoning: those spots also tend to be Reality Zones friendly to mysticism, and more hostile to high technology. &quot;Nuking&quot; such spots would be pretty damn Vulgar, even if no one was around to see it.<br /> <br /> That's assuming you even CAN &quot;nuke&quot; an extremely small area, like a single magickal site. I mean yes, the Technocracy could do that. But, again, Vulgar as hell, because nuclear weapons are pretty wide-ranging and indiscriminate in their destruction. This is established in the Consensus. If the Technocracy used extremely localized nukes, that would violate what the Consensus has to say about nuclear weapons. And if by &quot;nuke&quot;, you mean employ more exotic kinds of tactical weapons like orbital space lasers, that's EVEN MORE VULGAR than actual nukes, because orbital space lasers <i>are not a thing that exists</i> (yet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T01:54:37-07:00","id":1146941,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm not done. Let's continue, because there's so much wrong with this idea.<br /> <br /> Let's set aside the fact that most vampires Haven in cities, where orbital death rays blowing up buildings would definitely be noticed. Let's set aside the fact that Caerns are Nodes in everything but name, and the Technocracy would much rather take that resource for themselves, rather than damage it. Let's set aside that Trods are a Changeling thing, and most of the Union is skeptical that fairies even exist, let alone that they're a problem worth worrying about. Let's set aside that blowing up every haunted house or murder site is going to get noticed, and not all of those happen in remote areas. Let's set aside that Nephandi put a hell of a lot of effort into their Labyrinths, and may have wards against spells/technomagic of mass destruction. And let's certainly set aside that the Union, unless it investigates and infiltrates, has no idea what's in any of these places, and what or who might be caught in the blast radius.<br /> <br /> Let's set ALL OF THAT aside, and just examine the biggest reason why the Union doesn't nuke all its problems from orbit: it doesn't know where most of these places are, or even always WHAT they are.<br /> <br /> Night Folk a secretive by nature. They are basically a series of conspiracies that encompass entire species unto themselves. Like all good conspiracies, they seek to avoid being known as much as possible. Protecting their own versions of the Masquerade is constant with basically all of them, because they don't want to be found.<br /> <br /> Which means in a vast majority of cases, the Union has to work hard to find any of the sites mentioned, let alone ALL of them. The Union isn't even fully aware of how many vampires are running around - they underestimate their numbers. How would they know how many Havens are in a particular city, or where they are? Vast amounts of time and resources could be - and are - spent looking for individual sites significant to Reality Deviants. It's why the Traditions haven't been wiped off the face of the earth yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T01:57:05-07:00","id":1146942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1146938#post1146938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if that &quot;mass murdering atrocity&quot; means eradicating horrible, hideous monsters putting ISIS to shame?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's context dependant. In-setting the Technocracy did in fact use nuclear weapons against the Ravnos Antediluvian. So if the threat is big enough they will use them.<br /> <br /> But bear in mind the Technocracy already defeated the Nephandi and they probably think about the Nephandi in those terms. Why use weapons that murder thousands of innocent people when your foe is basically already defeated. Things might be different if the Technocracy were presently in an open war with the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Also, as I said, the Technocracy runs on secrecy and hypocrisy. If the higher ups start blatantly committing massive atrocities then the foot-soldiers of the Union are going to get rebellious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T02:05:05-07:00","id":1146944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1146942#post1146942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's context dependant. In-setting the Technocracy did in fact use nuclear weapons against the Ravnos Antediluvian. So if the threat is big enough they will use them.<br /> <br /> But bear in mind the Technocracy already defeated the Nephandi and they probably think about the Nephandi in those terms. Why use weapons that murder thousands of innocent people when your foe is basically already defeated. Things might be different if the Technocracy were presently in an open war with the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Also, as I said, the Technocracy runs on secrecy and hypocrisy. If the higher ups start blatantly committing massive atrocities then the foot-soldiers of the Union are going to get rebellious.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why bombarding isolated, depopulated(or non-habitat) area causes thousands of innocent death? Such indiscriminate carnage occurs when you nuke <i>cities</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T02:41:25-07:00","id":1146947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1146944#post1146944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why bombarding isolated, depopulated(or non-habitat) area causes thousands of innocent death? Such indiscriminate carnage occurs when you nuke <i>cities</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose they could in that case. That's just generally not where the monsters tend to gather; or to be exact, it's not where the monsters the Technocracy cares about are.<br /> <br /> I mean, a sleeping methuselah is extremely dangerous, but if it's asleep in some tomb in the middle of nowhere, who cares? The Technocracy has more pressing issues to deal with, and only limited resources.<br /> <br /> One other thing that I just realised. Your point about it being efficient is not quite right. The Technocrats are going to have to cover up the detonation which is going to be quite a bit of work, there's a lot of sleeper infrastructure designed to detect nuclear weapons. It's certainly doable, but it's still not something you do idly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T07:54:24-07:00","id":1147038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit#post1146919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the Union, especially Conventions like the Iteration X and the Void Engineers do not nuke every Haven, Caern, Pit, Hive, Haunts, Trods and Labyrinth from geostationary orbit? It is the simplest and most efficient and inexpensive(at least in terms of manpower and material losses) method to eradicate Methuselahs, Nephandi, BSD, Unseelie and other vile monstrosities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blueecho covered it pretty well.<br /> - First they even need to know where said secretive lair is.<br /> - Then they have to consider what is around it and what side-effects bombing it would have.<br /> - Then one might consider defenses or reactions to this activity. Some Methuselah (given I only know Vampire mechanics well) might survive a strike given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> Also, correct me if I'm wrong. Wasn't the Sixth Great Maelstrom caused by a technocrat blowing up a nuke in a Labyrinth?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T08:13:43-07:00","id":1147046,"title":"","content":"IIRC it was caused by the combination of a Primally Charged nuke destroying the avatars of those caught in the radius when they bombed the Ravnos antidilluvian. and an Etherite experimenting with nukes in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> In any case the answer is because none of these things are actually a threat. While the Traditions might view the union as their enemies in a great war for reality, the Union views all superstionists as the broken remnants of a defeated age.<br /> <br /> Their current operation isn't a war. They'd have to have a serious opponent for that. They view it as much closer to pest control or police work than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 10-05-2017, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T17:00:19-07:00","id":1147243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1146947#post1146947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose they could in that case. That's just generally not where the monsters tend to gather; or to be exact, it's not where the monsters the Technocracy cares about are.<br /> <br /> I mean, a sleeping methuselah is extremely dangerous, but if it's asleep in some tomb in the middle of nowhere, who cares? The Technocracy has more pressing issues to deal with, and only limited resources.<br /> <br /> One other thing that I just realised. Your point about it being efficient is not quite right. The Technocrats are going to have to cover up the detonation which is going to be quite a bit of work, there's a lot of sleeper infrastructure designed to detect nuclear weapons. It's certainly doable, but it's still not something you do idly.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's dancing around the bigger issue, which is that orbital space weapons would not be cheap to create and put into position. The Technocracy may have Magical Science, but their Paradigm is also beholden to Magical Economics. Because, remember, they have an entire Convention devoted to that.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's brand of engineering skews more towards the realistic when it comes to logistics, material and labor costs, and other factors. It isn't like the Society of Ether, who can produce war zeppelins or moon lasers, using nothing but junk and elbow grease. Building anything for the Union is an industrial project. Which tend to be expensive.<br /> <br /> Imagine for a moment that, in the Real World(TM), the US government had access to functional, practical laser weaponry. And that, with enough work and research, they could realize that type of weaponry on a massive scale. Let's say, further, that they could put one of those weapons in orbit.<br /> <br /> Are you really telling me that such a project would be <i>cheap</i>? That kind of thing would require a few billion dollars appended to the already bloated US defense budget <i>bare minimum</i>. Not even counting how many billions were spent beforehand in research and development. Actually building a space laser and rocketing it into orbit would cost, if I may borrow a British term, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULeDlxa3gyc\" target=\"_blank\">Loadsofmoney</a>.<br /> <br /> THAT is how the Technocracy does things, because they need to wrap their technomagick in a veneer of plausibility. Not even that, they legitimately believe that's how things must be done. It's part of the Union's collective Paradigm: technological answers to problems scale in expense to the scale of the problem. Which is why the Union doesn't have a legion of laser and nuke equipped satellites orbiting the Earth, no matter how much they might want one. And why they don't blow these kinds of weapon on any old nest of Reality Deviants.<br /> <br /> In this case, a strike team <i>really is</i> the more efficient method of dealing with such problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T19:17:53-07:00","id":1147282,"title":"","content":"Ummm.... &quot;Economy of scale&quot;. If they have the technology, they have an ENTIRE Convention that can make mass production, implementation and acceptance work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T19:30:29-07:00","id":1147292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1147282#post1147282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ummm.... &quot;Economy of scale&quot;. If they have the technology, they have an ENTIRE Convention that can make mass production, implementation and acceptance work.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it only works by making such things expensive. Especially if it's cutting edge research.<br /> <br /> Moreover, I would remind everyone that the Union, despite how much power and influence it has, does not have infinite resources. Even though the Union CAN authorize an unlimited budget, that is to be used only against threats against the entire world. Threats like a rampaging Antedeluvian. The Technocracy can't use that every day. It would destroy the world's economy, since you're flooding the money supply with a preposterous amount of (artificial) dosh. For normal purposes, there is only so many resources the Union is willing to use, and only certain things it will use those resources on. It may be on the order of billions of dollars, but it's still finite, and the Union wants to use those expenses wisely.<br /> <br /> They aren't going to blow their extremely expensive orbital death lasers or space weapons platforms on one nest of lycanthropes. In the same way you don't use valuable ammunition to shoot rats in the walls. Pest control is what rat poison and mouse traps are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T04:20:15-07:00","id":1147361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1146939#post1146939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem with that reasoning: those spots also tend to be Reality Zones friendly to mysticism, and more hostile to high technology. &quot;Nuking&quot; such spots would be pretty damn Vulgar, even if no one was around to see it.<br /> <br /> That's assuming you even CAN &quot;nuke&quot; an extremely small area, like a single magickal site. I mean yes, the Technocracy could do that. But, again, Vulgar as hell, because nuclear weapons are pretty wide-ranging and indiscriminate in their destruction. This is established in the Consensus. If the Technocracy used extremely localized nukes, that would violate what the Consensus has to say about nuclear weapons. And if by &quot;nuke&quot;, you mean employ more exotic kinds of tactical weapons like orbital space lasers, that's EVEN MORE VULGAR than actual nukes, because orbital space lasers <i>are not a thing that exists</i> (yet).</div> </div> </div> </div>But why that is &quot;Vulgar as hell&quot; if you nuke remote areas? And nuclear weapons are firmly accepted in Consensus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1147243#post1147243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's dancing around the bigger issue, which is that orbital space weapons would not be cheap to create and put into position. The Technocracy may have Magical Science, but their Paradigm is also beholden to Magical Economics. Because, remember, they have an entire Convention devoted to that.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's brand of engineering skews more towards the realistic when it comes to logistics, material and labor costs, and other factors. It isn't like the Society of Ether, who can produce war zeppelins or moon lasers, using nothing but junk and elbow grease. Building anything for the Union is an industrial project. Which tend to be expensive.<br /> <br /> Imagine for a moment that, in the Real World(TM), the US government had access to functional, practical laser weaponry. And that, with enough work and research, they could realize that type of weaponry on a massive scale. Let's say, further, that they could put one of those weapons in orbit.<br /> <br /> Are you really telling me that such a project would be <i>cheap</i>? That kind of thing would require a few billion dollars appended to the already bloated US defense budget <i>bare minimum</i>. Not even counting how many billions were spent beforehand in research and development. Actually building a space laser and rocketing it into orbit would cost, if I may borrow a British term, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULeDlxa3gyc\" target=\"_blank\">Loadsofmoney</a>.<br /> <br /> THAT is how the Technocracy does things, because they need to wrap their technomagick in a veneer of plausibility. Not even that, they legitimately believe that's how things must be done. It's part of the Union's collective Paradigm: technological answers to problems scale in expense to the scale of the problem. Which is why the Union doesn't have a legion of laser and nuke equipped satellites orbiting the Earth, no matter how much they might want one. And why they don't blow these kinds of weapon on any old nest of Reality Deviants.<br /> <br /> In this case, a strike team <i>really is</i> the more efficient method of dealing with such problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>And why that is so expensive? They simply utilize already manufactured, equipped <i>and </i>launched orbital defense satellites and weapon platforms? Which they have a <i>lot</i>, and featuring diverse designs and purposes, even if calling that &quot;a legion&quot; might be a bit stretch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T07:09:09-07:00","id":1147398,"title":"","content":"To set aside questions of expense and logistics - remember that the Union is playing for the Consensus. They need Sleepers to believe the world is static, well-understood, and scientifically understood. Disrupting that pleasant dream is the <i>worst possible result</i> for the Union. Why would they want to get down in the mud with the rest of these vulgar Reality Deviants? That would sacrifice all they've built for the last millennium. Tons of nukes is nearly as disruptive as tons of fire elementals.<br /> <br /> Think of the Union as trying to fight its enemies in a house without waking the sleeping occupants. Discretion is the better part of valor, especially when they believe that their carefully maintained Consensus will eventually wipe away all these Deviants because no one will believe in them. <br /> <br /> So - what enemies really threaten the Consensus? A vampire quietly feeding in New York City and occasionally exsanguinating a homeless guy and leaving him in a dumpster isn't a threat, and the Union isn't in the business of defending every single human life. A vampire who's already started killing half the people on the Indian subcontinent - well, that's a pretty big threat. To use the metaphor - he's already woken up everyone in the house, so bring out the big guns.<br /> <br /> Most of the enemies you described aren't major threats to the Consensus because they keep to themselves and are themselves invested in staying hidden. Blatancy is what will bring out the orbital death rays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T11:50:17-07:00","id":1147511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1147292#post1147292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it only works by making such things expensive. Especially if it's cutting edge research.<br /> <br /> Moreover, I would remind everyone that the Union, despite how much power and influence it has, does not have infinite resources. Even though the Union CAN authorize an unlimited budget, that is to be used only against threats against the entire world. Threats like a rampaging Antedeluvian. The Technocracy can't use that every day. It would destroy the world's economy, since you're flooding the money supply with a preposterous amount of (artificial) dosh. For normal purposes, there is only so many resources the Union is willing to use, and only certain things it will use those resources on. It may be on the order of billions of dollars, but it's still finite, and the Union wants to use those expenses wisely.<br /> <br /> They aren't going to blow their extremely expensive orbital death lasers or space weapons platforms on one nest of lycanthropes. In the same way you don't use valuable ammunition to shoot rats in the walls. Pest control is what rat poison and mouse traps are for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly the OPPOSITE of how economy of scale works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T13:31:23-07:00","id":1147563,"title":"","content":"The issue with the whole &quot;Economy of Scale&quot; argument is that noone likes the Syndicate. The two main constructors of Void Ships and Orbital Battle Stations are the Void Engineers and to a lesser degree Iteration X.<br /> <br /> The Iteration X is firmly on the side of the NWO in the rifts that currently plague the Union and consider the Syndicate a bunch of useless cowards. And the Void Engineers don't trust anyone from the Mudball because of Threat Null.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate would, could, and DOES demand eyes on anything that costs that much of their money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T15:51:29-07:00","id":1147600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1147563#post1147563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with the whole &quot;Economy of Scale&quot; argument is that noone likes the Syndicate. The two main constructors of Void Ships and Orbital Battle Stations are the Void Engineers and to a lesser degree Iteration X.<br /> <br /> The Iteration X is firmly on the side of the NWO in the rifts that currently plague the Union and consider the Syndicate a bunch of useless cowards. And the Void Engineers don't trust anyone from the Mudball because of Threat Null.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate would, could, and DOES demand eyes on anything that costs that much of their money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm.... Then the VE's are stone cold stupid. The NWO is their enemy. They spend huge amounts of resources that COULD be used in the fight against Threat Null in undoing Conditioning and even more in dancing around the NWO finding it out. And if they ever do... WHEN they do, then it's a two front fight for the VE's. Threat Null over here and the NWO's who only understand the entire VE Convention is in clandestine rebellion vs. the Union. (And two front wars don't go well when you are in a tenable position. Which they aren't.) <br /> <br /> Those are their &quot;friends&quot;. Oh and there are exactly 0 NWO agents helping out the VEs with anything they deem important. So... Big help there. The Syndicate may want eyes, but the NWO IS the eyes. <br /> <br /> The Syndicate on the other hand, has EXACTLY what the VE's need to keep the fighting going. Not only are they the masters of logistics (which allow the VE's to actually fight... since even being a mage doesn't make mobilizing an armed forces without logistical support anything other than a losing proposition), but they have access to the one thing that the VE's need in bulk, Quint. Sure they may be able to grab a few Nodes and throw the odd EDE into a conversion furnace, but, to win a war, the VEs need those Void Ships and Battle Stations. And only the Syndicate, ONLY them, can actually have the production process of a Void Ship production line generate the Quint needed to make the ship anything other than a cool spaceship sculpture. In fact if the VE's want to have a chance at winning it's out-producing Threat Null. They have Earth as a resource base. To WIN, the VE's need the Syndicate and It-X. <br /> <br /> The NWO does not have access to the resources to be of any real use. They don't offer anything the VE's can't do on their own just as well or better and they are ACTIVELY opposed to and investigating the VE's for what they are doing. <br /> <br /> And that's STILL not how economy of scale works. They Syndicate may be the best at it, but everyone in the Union uses it. What the Hell do you think the Time-Motion Managers are doing? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T19:18:59-07:00","id":1147641,"title":"","content":"I'm not even sure what you're arguing. The VE Don't Like the NWO. This was fairly clear. They're willing to work with the Syndicate to a limited degree, but still don't like doing so, and violently rebuff any oversight.<br /> <br /> And no, the Syndicate is not NECESSARY for the creation of voidcraft. A useful shortcut? Sure. But not necessary.<br /> <br /> The Time Motion Managers are predicting the future. I think you're thinking of the Macrotechnicians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T10:34:34-07:00","id":1148055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1147641#post1147641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sure what you're arguing. The VE Don't Like the NWO. This was fairly clear. They're willing to work with the Syndicate to a limited degree, but still don't like doing so, and violently rebuff any oversight.<br /> <br /> And no, the Syndicate is not NECESSARY for the creation of voidcraft. A useful shortcut? Sure. But not necessary.<br /> <br /> The Time Motion Managers are predicting the future. I think you're thinking of the Macrotechnicians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is the Quint coming from? Using the amounts needed (based on the VE-rev book) is a crippling huge amount. Particularly when the only source outside the Syndicate (that can MAKE Quint) is pretty much Nodes. On Earth. Where the VEs have minimal presence and minimal influence. Requests for that amount of Quint are going to come back stamped &quot;DENIED&quot;. (Oh, I guess the VEs could waste a bunch of mages as batteries in a Matrix set-up and extract Quint from them. And there's always grinding up EDE's for fuel. But neither of those are going to produce the amount needed for assembly line production of Void Ships, which is what you NEED to win a war.) No the Syndicate is not NECESSARY for the production of A Void Ship here and there. They are ESSENTIAL for the production of enough Void Ships to fight a war.<br /> <br /> Your Technocracy isn't really a Union is it? It's five competing factions that are at each other's throats under a thin gloss of some kind of mission statement so vague as to be meaningless. It makes the Traditions and Alliance look like models of cooperative efficiency. If every faction is actually 100% functionally independent then, considering they really don't even have a coherent shared ideology under this conception, what is keeping them together? Institutional inertia? The Union may have issues between the Conventions, but it still seems to be WORKING. There may be a management crisis on the horizon but that doesn't mean the company is going to stop working. (And/or they whole company may have been co-opted by corporate pirate nihilist anarchist that are trying to use it as a tool to crash the global economy... and it's STILL working, until that moment when its dark masters want to blow it up and crash the world....)<br /> <br /> Which means that the various bits are doing their parts of a long term large scale project: The VEs are the start and end. They make the request from Control (carefully couched to make it seems like they are dealing with Avatar Storm aftermath... which works because it really isn't entirely untrue). After some scrutiny (largely by the NWO with Syndicate input), the plans get approved and It-X and the Syndicate work out the logistics for the large scale production. The VEs take possession of the completed products. The VEs are probably getting substantially less than they really need as they have to lowball the request to keep it from pinging the &quot;WTF are they doing?&quot; radar of the approval committee, which is, in turn, almost certainly giving only a fraction of what is asked for. Is there a Syndicate rep in the shipyard making sure the allocated resources are being used appropriately. But that's pretty much an accounting issue, not oversight. (So don't give them any red flags to have them call in the auditors...) Are the VEs trying to build, re-build what they can on the side? Sure. Are they probably even seizing and retasking compatible SoE ships and manning them with VEs who have to use Hypertech to figure what the buttons even do? Probably. But that's a whole lot different from a completely separate VE building a whole armada of ships with resources and knowhow they really don't have to the degree necessary. They need a (new, reconfured) FLEET not a new ship now and then where they can eek one out.<br /> <br /> And that's not what the Time-Motion Managers do. They do what I said they do. They are the experts in cybernetics (original meaning of the word.) They are the lineal descendants of Henry Ford's assembly line efficiency model. The one that proved the concept of economy of scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 10-08-2017, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T12:47:54-07:00","id":1148094,"title":"","content":"They DON'T have an assembly line of ships. This is more or less Explicitly stated in Void Engineer Rev. They bring in old destroyed ships, and retrofit them to function again. There are 4 Qui La Machinae in the ENTIRE VE fleet. Why? because they were in drydock when the Avatar storm hit.<br /> <br /> Or alternatively, from machinery that creates quintessence, the mechanical details of which I've posted before, and of which there are examples of in the books themselves.<br /> <br /> It's not even that, the VE have been noted renegades for a long time in the fluff. Pointing out that the Renegades are Renegades and the Corrupt are the Corrupt still leaves you with more than half of the conventions who are functional.<br /> <br /> No, that's idiotic. The Original Meaning of the Word Cybernetics is &quot;Treating Biological structures as if they were mechanical structures.&quot; Yes, the flashy robot arms are the result of that, but so are things like surgery.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T07:30:20-07:00","id":1148295,"title":"","content":"Economics will ALWAYS be a big factor and primary answer. Scarcity is a fact of life, even for people as capable of blatantly humiliating thermodynamics as magi.<br /> Why nuke something if there is a non-nuke solution? Most often nothing is a big enough threat to warrant that, and even then you still have to ponder on billionaire expenditures and the inevitable obscene collateral damage...<br /> <br /> <br /> It's just not worth it. Too many expenses, too many things to go wrong, most often there are plenty alternatives.<br /> <br /> When there *aren't*, then you speak of nukes. It happened once or twice and it required a ravnos antediluvian. Don't expect a smaller problem to be answered with mass destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T08:42:39-07:00","id":1148321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146919-why-the-union-does-not-nuke-its-enemies-from-orbit?p=1148094#post1148094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They DON'T have an assembly line of ships. This is more or less Explicitly stated in Void Engineer Rev. They bring in old destroyed ships, and retrofit them to function again. There are 4 Qui La Machinae in the ENTIRE VE fleet. Why? because they were in drydock when the Avatar storm hit.<br /> <br /> Or alternatively, from machinery that creates quintessence, the mechanical details of which I've posted before, and of which there are examples of in the books themselves.<br /> <br /> It's not even that, the VE have been noted renegades for a long time in the fluff. Pointing out that the Renegades are Renegades and the Corrupt are the Corrupt still leaves you with more than half of the conventions who are functional.<br /> <br /> No, that's idiotic. The Original Meaning of the Word Cybernetics is &quot;Treating Biological structures as if they were mechanical structures.&quot; Yes, the flashy robot arms are the result of that, but so are things like surgery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they better GET one. Or they are going to LOSE.<br /> <br /> But they don't need to get one. They have one. There is nothing that says that that is the only way they are getting ships. At all. Salvage and retrofitting are a big part and can be hidden better by cooking the books and under-reporting. (Oh, and that is also fundamentally the same thing as creation of new ships as far as logistics goes. It's just a slightly different pipeline.) As directly stated and heavily implied by the fact there is whole section on making Void Ships and the costs of operating them. As well as pointing out that they have 4 Qui La ships. Why don't they have four idiosyncratic ships that sorta do the same things. SOMEONE produced those as ships of the line. Meaning there is such thing as standadrized ships of the line. And, this is the big one, guess what the word &quot;dry dock&quot; means? It means the shipyards where Void Ships are maintained and created. And they survived the Event to the level that they were able to protect those four ships. So.... why aren't they using them for their created purpose?<br /> <br /> I guess, if you want your VE to be that hard up and Conventional Space to be pretty much completely out of Union control with a Battlestar Galactica like fleet of rag-tag ships trying to make do in the face of odds they can't beat (particularly since the VE mission isn't &quot;Bug out and live&quot;, it's &quot;Attack the enemy you can't beat and die&quot;), then bully for you. But that's not the story that's going down in the VE-rev book or the appropriate parts of M20 so far. The VEs are rocked back on their heels, but they have made adjustments and are trying not just to hold the line but to find some way to win.<br /> <br /> Renegades means they are operating in theaters outside of normal NWO and Syndicate channels of control on a day-to-day basis. It doens't mean they are a completely separate organization with it's own complete internal organization. The point of the Union is synergy. Each Convention is relying on the others to do they things they are best at so they can use that expertise to further their own mission. Hence &quot;Union&quot;. And, precisely, the &quot;renegades&quot; aren't really renegades. Not even as much as separates them as does every Tradition from each other. They are still part of the system, but they are the part of the system that causes eye-rolling and head-shaking, but is allowed because their &quot;renegade&quot; nature is the best fit for them to do their job as dictated by Control and as necessitated by the Time Line.<br /> <br /> That is NOT what cybernetics means. That's what people think it means because that's the way it falls into the zeitgeist by way of sci-fi. It's like &quot;discrimination&quot; and &quot;synthetic&quot; which have layers of meaning added on to the original that obscure what it means when used in the way it was intended. That meaning is a particularization of a branch of one part of the meaning that is accepted when discussing the overall discipline of cybernetics. As in &quot;Cybernetics is what a cybernetician does&quot;. It's not just or even mostly making cyborgs. It's minutely that. You don't have to go very far to find this out. Even Wikipedia doesn't really water it down. What the word cybernetics means in the sense of the Time-Motion Managers is exactly what I said it is and my comment wasn't idiotic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 10-09-2017, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}